---
layout: base.njk
title: SDET Engineering Playbook
description: From Selenium Automation to AI-Enabled Quality Engineering — a practical engineering knowledge base and interview preparation platform.
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
<div class="home">
  <section class="home-hero">
    <p class="home-hero__eyebrow">SDET Engineering Playbook</p>
    <h1 class="home-hero__title">From Selenium Automation to AI-Enabled Quality Engineering</h1>
    <p class="home-hero__tagline">A practical engineering knowledge base covering Java, Selenium 4, framework design, API and database testing, CI/CD, Playwright, and the AI era of quality engineering — built to read like a technical book.</p>
    <div class="home-hero__cta">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ '/roadmap/' | url }}">Start the roadmap</a>
      <a class="btn" href="{{ '/selenium/explicit-waits/' | url }}">Read a sample chapter</a>
      <a class="btn" href="{{ '/interview/practice/' | url }}">Interview practice</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  {# Continue reading — populated client-side from localStorage. #}
  <section class="home-section" data-continue-section hidden>
    <h2>Continue reading</h2>
    <div data-continue-card></div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Your progress</h2>
    <div class="stat-row">
      <div class="meter"><span class="meter__fill" data-progress-fill></span></div>
      <span class="stat-row__value" data-progress-value>0%</span>
    </div>
    <p class="home-hero__tagline" style="font-size:0.9rem;margin-top:var(--space-3)">Progress and bookmarks are stored locally in your browser. No account required.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Explore the playbook</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      {% for group in collections.nav %}
        {% for cat in group.categories %}
        <a class="card" href="{{ cat.articles[0].url | url }}">
          <h3>{{ cat.label }}</h3>
          <p>{{ cat.articles.length }} article{% if cat.articles.length != 1 %}s{% endif %} · {{ group.label }}</p>
        </a>
        {% endfor %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
